# The frozen mock examples are compared to a fresh `--mock` run byte for byte
# (`test_*_committed_example_matches_a_fresh_mock_run`, one per trial script).
# That comparison is `read_bytes()`, so the line endings on disk have to match
# what the writer emits, on every platform.
#
# PAIRED WITH `newline="\n"` IN `scripts/_trial_common.py` (`write_report`, and
# `snapshot_writer`). Removing this line REQUIRES reverting those, and vice
# versa -- either one alone leaves a broken state:
#
#   * this line without the writer change -> checkout gives LF everywhere, but
#     `write_text` with `newline=None` still emits CRLF on Windows, so every
#     example test fails on every Windows machine;
#   * the writer change without this line -> the writer emits LF everywhere,
#     but `core.autocrlf=true` smudges the checkout to CRLF on Windows, so the
#     same tests fail the same way, mirrored.
#
# Before this file existed the invariant held only because both conversions
# happened to key off the same platform and agree. That made it a property of
# each contributor's git config rather than of the repository: one Windows
# contributor with `core.autocrlf=false` commits a CRLF blob, and all the
# example tests go red at once with a cause that appears in no diff.
trial-reports/examples/** text eol=lf
